### =========================================================================
### Distributed Payment Gateway - Complete End-to-End API Test Suite
### Base Gateway URL: http://localhost:8080
### =========================================================================

### 1. Register a Customer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sarah Connor",
  "email": "sarah.connor@cyberdyne.com",
  "phone": "+14155552671"
}

### 2. Register a Merchant (Generates API Key)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/merchants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cyberdyne Systems",
  "email": "billing@cyberdyne.com"
}

### 3. Create a Payment (Authorized with X-API-Key and Idempotency-Key)
# Note: Replace the X-API-Key value with the apiKey returned in Step 2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key
Idempotency-Key: pay_order_001_unique_key

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "merchantId": 1,
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 4. Replay Same Payment Request (Idempotency Replay -> Returns original payment without double charge)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key
Idempotency-Key: pay_order_001_unique_key

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "merchantId": 1,
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 5. Send Same Idempotency Key with Modified Payload (Triggers 422 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key
Idempotency-Key: pay_order_001_unique_key

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "merchantId": 1,
  "amount": 999.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 6. Test Payment Provider Failure Simulation (Amount ending in .91 triggers INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key
Idempotency-Key: pay_insufficient_funds_test

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "merchantId": 1,
  "amount": 50.91,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 7. Issue Partial Refund #1 ($30.00 on $100.00 Payment)
# Replace {paymentRef} with actual paymentReference (e.g. pay_...)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments/pay_example_ref/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key

{
  "amount": 30.00,
  "reason": "Customer returned partial item"
}

### 8. Issue Partial Refund #2 ($20.00 on remaining $70.00)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments/pay_example_ref/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key

{
  "amount": 20.00,
  "reason": "Defective discount adjustment"
}

### 9. Attempt Over-Refund ($60.00 on remaining $50.00 -> Triggers 400 INVALID_REFUND_REQUEST)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments/pay_example_ref/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key

{
  "amount": 60.00,
  "reason": "Exceeding available balance"
}

### 10. Check Refund Summary (Original: $100, Total Refunded: $50, Remaining: $50)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments/pay_example_ref/refunds/summary
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key

### 11. Final Refund ($50.00 settling entire payment to REFUNDED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments/pay_example_ref/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: mcht_live_example_key

{
  "amount": 50.00,
  "reason": "Full settlement"
}

### 12. Query Dispatched Notifications History
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/notifications

### 13. Query Immutable Audit Trail Timeline for Payment
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/audit-events/aggregate/pay_example_ref
